**Describe the bug**

Since last week (Exact date 19.February) my Meshcentral server is behaving strangely. I cannot connect to WEB GUI, as immediatelly after entering login detail I have message "Server Disconnected".  I completely reinstalled the server sevceral times, but it helped only for couple of minutes. I went bacx from ver 1.21 to stable 1.1.0 but same issue.

I have been using MC last 3 years with the same config, always used to have automatic update, and literally I have not touched the MC server in last 6 months, so I do not think I could be in wrong settings...  I switched the autoupdates off for debugging reasons now. But the disconnected message still appreares, even on Stable version 1.1.0.

When I delete all folders and re-install the server, it runs well for couple of minutes, but after 5 minutes or so the issue is comming back again. And all I can see is "Server disconnected"

Fortunatelly I had a working backup (full installation folder, not only data folder) and by comparing files I realised what is causing the issue  -  after some time the file package.json changes, respective one character "**^**" is added - the line No. 6 (meshcentral) which causes the "disconnection" of the server.

working version of packages.json looks like this:
```

{
  "dependencies": {
    "acme-client": "^4.2.5",
    "archiver": "^5.3.1",
    "loadavg-windows": "1.1.1",
    "meshcentral": "1.1.0",
    "node-windows": "^0.1.4",
    "otplib": "10.2.3"
  }
}

```
but after couple of minutes this file is changed into:

```
{
  "dependencies": {
    "acme-client": "^4.2.5",
    "archiver": "^5.3.1",
    "loadavg-windows": "1.1.1",
    "meshcentral": "^1.1.0",                                 <-- this is the problematic line
    "node-windows": "^0.1.4",
    "otplib": "10.2.3"
  }
}

```

if I delete the "^" sign and restart the meshcentral service, the web gui starts immediatelly, but after couple of minutes it says again "Server Disconnected" and I have to delete ^ again and restart.

I found a workaround, but this is not a solution: Lock the file so that it does not get overwritten with ^ line....

 First I deleted "^" and marked the packages.json as read-only file, but this did not help and despite of read-only attribute, meshcentral was still overwriting the file with "a bad line with ^".
 
So I had to remove write permissions from this file for "system user" and now only Administrator can change it. As Meshcentral is running as a windows service, it does not use Administrator account and therefore now Meshcentral does not have the right to change the paskages.json file and since then I did not have any disconnection...



