Why this broke in Angular 18.2.14

Angular introduced BootstrapContext for server bootstrapping (because of [GHSA-68x2-mx4q-78m7](https://github.com/advisories/GHSA-68x2-mx4q-78m7)
).

This changed the behavior of getPlatform() and destroyPlatform() → they now return null.

Apps relying on these APIs (common in SSR with platformServer + TransferState) fail after upgrading from 18.2.13 → 18.2.14.

Workarounds
Option 1 – Quick Fix (downgrade)

If you just want your SSR app working quickly without refactoring, pin Angular to 18.2.13:

npm install @angular/core@18.2.13 @angular/platform-server@18.2.13


Not recommended long-term (you’ll miss security patches).

Option 2 – Proper Fix (refactor to BootstrapContext)

Instead of getPlatform() and destroyPlatform(), you should migrate to the new SSR bootstrapping APIs.

Before (old style):

import { getPlatform, destroyPlatform } from '@angular/core';
import { platformServer } from '@angular/platform-server';
import { AppServerModule } from './app/app.server.module';

export function render(): Promise<string> {
  const platform = platformServer();
  return platform.bootstrapModule(AppServerModule).then(appRef => {
    // This breaks after 18.2.14
    const platformRef = getPlatform();
    destroyPlatform();
    return '<html>...</html>';
  });
}


After (new style with BootstrapContext):

import { bootstrapApplication } from '@angular/platform-browser';
import { provideServerRendering, renderApplication } from '@angular/platform-server';
import { AppComponent } from './app/app.component';

export async function render(): Promise<string> {
  return await renderApplication(() => 
    bootstrapApplication(AppComponent, {
      providers: [
        provideServerRendering()
      ]
    })
  );
}


renderApplication() handles the full SSR lifecycle.

 BootstrapContext is used internally, no need to call getPlatform() / destroyPlatform().

Works with TransferState out of the box.

 Migration Notes

Stop using getPlatform() / destroyPlatform() → no longer supported after 18.2.14.

Switch to bootstrapApplication() + renderApplication() for SSR entry points.

If using TransferState, import it normally:

import { TransferState } from '@angular/platform-browser';


and Angular will serialize/deserialize between server ↔ client automatically.

