issues.body:
# 9.1.1 regression: wildcard handler change breaks `@fastify/swagger-ui` encapsulation

## Summary

`@fastify/static@9.1.1` rewrote the wildcard route handler to derive the file path from `req.raw.url` (via a new `getPathnameForSend(url, prefix)` helper) instead of `req.params['*']`. The new helper only strips the *plugin-local* prefix, so when `@fastify/static` is registered inside another plugin's encapsulation (e.g. `@fastify/swagger-ui` registers it under its own `/static` scope), all asset routes 404 with `"Route not found"` even though the file exists on disk.

## Reproduction

Minimal reproduction below — copy the three files into a directory and run `pnpm install && pnpm exec tsx test.ts`:

`server.ts`:

```ts
import path from 'node:path';
import { fileURLToPath } from 'node:url';
import Fastify from 'fastify';
import fastifyStatic from '@fastify/static';
import swagger from '@fastify/swagger';
import swaggerUi from '@fastify/swagger-ui';

const __dirname = path.dirname(fileURLToPath(import.meta.url));

const app = Fastify();
await app.register(swagger, { openapi: { info: { title: 'repro', version: '0.0.0' }, paths: {} } });
await app.register(swaggerUi, { routePrefix: '/docs' });
await app.register(fastifyStatic, {
  root: path.join(__dirname, 'uploads'),
  prefix: '/uploads/',
  decorateReply: false,
});
await app.listen({ port: 3000 });
```

`package.json`:

```json
{
  "type": "module",
  "dependencies": {
    "fastify": "5.2.0",
    "@fastify/static": "9.1.1",
    "@fastify/swagger": "9.7.0",
    "@fastify/swagger-ui": "5.2.5"
  }
}
```

Then:

```
curl -i http://localhost:3000/docs/static/swagger-ui.css
```

## Expected behaviour (works on 9.1.0)

```
HTTP/1.1 200 OK
content-type: text/css; charset=UTF-8
…
```

## Actual behaviour on 9.1.1

```
HTTP/1.1 404 Not Found
{"message":"Route GET:/docs/static/swagger-ui.css not found","error":"Not Found","statusCode":404}
```

Tested four probes against an otherwise-identical setup, swapping only the `@fastify/static` version:

| Probe | Path | 9.1.0 | 9.1.1 |
|---|---|---|---|
| Swagger UI HTML root | `/docs/` | 200 ✓ | 200 ✓ |
| CSS asset under encapsulation | `/docs/static/swagger-ui.css` | 200 ✓ | **404** ✗ |
| JS asset under encapsulation | `/docs/static/swagger-ui-bundle.js` | 200 ✓ | **404** ✗ |
| Independent fastify-static mount (control) | `/uploads/test.txt` | 200 ✓ | 200 ✓ |

The `/docs/` HTML root (served by an inline route inside swagger-ui itself) still renders, but every asset under `/docs/static/*` returns 404.

A non-encapsulated `@fastify/static` mount on the same app (e.g. `/uploads/test.txt`) continues to work on both 9.1.0 and 9.1.1 — confirming the regression is specifically the encapsulated case.

## Bisected to

`index.js`, lines 122–128 in 9.1.0 → 122–133 in 9.1.1. The wildcard route handler changed:

**9.1.0** (works):

```js
handler (req, reply) {
  pumpSendToReply(req, reply, '/' + req.params['*'], sendOptions.root)
}
```

**9.1.1** (regresses):

```js
handler (req, reply) {
  const pathname = getPathnameForSend(req.raw.url, prefix)
  if (!pathname) {
    return reply.callNotFound()
  }
  pumpSendToReply(req, reply, pathname, sendOptions.root)
}
```

Where the new helper (added at `index.js:570`+) only strips the plugin-local `prefix` from `req.raw.url`:

```js
function getPathnameForSend (url, prefix) {
  // … question-mark trim …
  if (prefix !== '/') {
    const routePrefix = prefix.endsWith('/') ? prefix.slice(0, -1) : prefix
    if (!pathname.startsWith(routePrefix)) {
      return    // ← undefined → handler 404s
    }
    pathname = pathname.slice(routePrefix.length)
  }
  return pathname
}
```

When invoked from inside `@fastify/swagger-ui`'s encapsulation:
- `req.raw.url` = `/docs/static/swagger-ui.css` (the full request path)
- `prefix` = `/static` (the plugin-local prefix that `@fastify/swagger-ui` passed when it registered `@fastify/static` inside its own scope)
- `pathname.startsWith('/static')` is **false** because the full URL starts with `/docs/static/…`, not `/static/…`
- `getPathnameForSend` returns `undefined`
- Handler calls `reply.callNotFound()`

The 9.1.0 approach (`req.params['*']`) was encapsulation-safe because Fastify's router populates `params['*']` relative to the matched route, which already accounts for any parent encapsulation prefix. The 9.1.1 approach assumes `prefix` reflects the full request-time path prefix, which it doesn't when the plugin is registered nested.

The path-traversal hardening that 9.1.1 also shipped (in `lib/dirList.js`, the new `isPathInsideRoot` guard — addressing CVE-2026-6410) is independent of the wildcard-handler change and is unaffected by reverting just the route handler.

## Workaround

Pin to 9.1.0 via your package manager's overrides mechanism. For pnpm:

```jsonc
// package.json
{
  "pnpm": {
    "overrides": {
      "@fastify/static": "9.1.0"
    }
  }
}
```

The CVE-2026-6410 directory-listing path-traversal exposure that 9.1.1 fixes is irrelevant for any registration that doesn't pass `list: true` (off by default).

## Suggested fix direction

Restore the 9.1.0 wildcard handler (use `req.params['*']`), and add the directory-listing path-traversal hardening (`isPathInsideRoot`) as a separate change to `lib/dirList.js`. The two patches are orthogonal.

## Environment

- Node 20.20.2 (also reproduced under Node 22.x in CI)
- macOS 14 / Linux x86_64
- pnpm 9.15.9
- Fastify 5.2.0, `@fastify/swagger` 9.7.0, `@fastify/swagger-ui` 5.2.5

### Prerequisites

- [x] I have written a descriptive issue title
- [x] I have searched existing issues to ensure the regression has not already been reported


### Last working version

9.1.0

### Stopped working in version

9.1.1

### Node.js version

22.22.0

### Operating system

macOS

### Operating system version (i.e. 20.04, 11.3, 10)

15.7.4

### 💥 Regression Report

Fastify 9.1.1 and 9.1.2 replies with 404 when the configured prefix contains a param e.g. `/app/:version`.

Fastify 9.1.0 works as expected.

### Steps to Reproduce

The following sample test works fine in 9.1.0 and fails with 9.1.1 and 9.1.2.

```typescript
import assert from 'node:assert';
import fastify from 'fastify';
import fastifyStatic from '@fastify/static';
import fs from 'node:fs/promises';
import { test } from 'node:test';

/**
 * Regression test for @fastify/static@9.1.1 issue
 * 9.1.0: ✅ Works correctly
 * 9.1.1: ❌ Returns 404
 * 9.1.2: ❌ Returns 404
 */
await test('fastify-static should serve files when prefix contains param', async () => {
  const root = import.meta.dirname;
  const filename = import.meta.filename.slice(root.length + 1);
  const fileContent = await fs.readFile(import.meta.filename, 'utf8');

  const app = fastify();
  await app.register(fastifyStatic, { root, prefix: '/app/:version' });
  await app.ready();

  const response = await app.inject({
    method: 'GET',
    url: `/app/1.2.3/${filename}`,
  });

  assert.equal(response.statusCode, 200);
  assert.equal(response.body, fileContent);
});
```

### Expected Behavior

_No response_

### Prerequisites

