issues.body:
Vite dev middleware swallows asset-extensioned URLs (`.jpg`/`.png`/…) even when a Nitro route matches — `req._nitroHandled` is set unconditionally in `nitroDevMiddlewarePre`.

### Environment

- `nitro@3.0.260429-beta`
- `vite@8.0.11`
- `h3@2.0.1-rc.22`
- Node 24 / macOS

### Summary

When the Nitro Vite plugin is in use, the dev server intercepts any URL whose extension matches the built-in `ASSET_EXT_RE` (jsx/tsx/png/**jpg**/svg/webp/avif/woff2/…) and routes it to Vite's static middleware *even if a user-defined Nitro route matches the URL*. The intercept also poisons the late-stage Nitro fallback by setting `req._nitroHandled = true`, so the request never gets a chance to reach the user's route handler. Vite's `serve-static@2.x` then emits the canonical `404 + Content-Security-Policy: default-src 'none' + X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff`.

URLs without an extension, or with extensions not in `ASSET_EXT_RE` (e.g. `.txt`), reach the route handler normally. This produces a confusing asymmetry where `/api/photos/12345.jpg` 404s but `/api/photos/12345.txt` works.

### Reproduction

Minimal vanilla repro (no TanStack Start / Nuxt / etc. needed):

`package.json`
```json
{
  "name": "nitro-static-demo",
  "private": true,
  "type": "module",
  "scripts": { "dev": "vite" },
  "devDependencies": {
    "h3": "2.0.1-rc.22",
    "nitro": "3.0.260429-beta",
    "vite": "^8.0.10"
  }
}
```

`vite.config.ts`
```ts
import { defineConfig } from "vite";
import { nitro } from "nitro/vite";
export default defineConfig({ plugins: [nitro()] });
```

`nitro.config.ts`
```ts
import { defineConfig } from "nitro/config";
export default defineConfig({ scanDirs: ["."] });
```

`routes/api/photos/[...].ts`
```ts
import { defineEventHandler } from "h3";
export default defineEventHandler((event) => ({
  handlerReached: true,
  url: event.url?.pathname ?? event.path,
  params: event.context.params,
}));
```

Then:
```sh
pnpm install && pnpm dev
curl -si http://localhost:3000/api/photos/12345        # 200, handler reached
curl -si http://localhost:3000/api/photos/12345.txt    # 200, handler reached
curl -si http://localhost:3000/api/photos/12345.jpg    # 404 with `Content-Security-Policy: default-src 'none'`
```

### Bisect

Same project, only the `nitro` version changed:

| `nitro` version | `/api/photos/12345` | `/api/photos/12345.txt` | `/api/photos/12345.jpg` |
| --- | --- | --- | --- |
| `3.0.1-alpha.2` | 200 | 200 | **200** |
| `3.0.260429-beta` | 200 | 200 | **404 (serve-static@2.x)** |

Vite version held constant at 8.0.11. Reverting Vite alone does not fix it; reverting Nitro alone does. So this is a Nitro regression introduced between `3.0.1-alpha.2` and `3.0.260429-beta`.

### Root cause

`nitro/dist/vite.mjs`, in the `nitroDevMiddlewarePre` middleware:

```js
// nitro/dist/vite.mjs (3.0.260429-beta)
const ASSET_EXT_RE = /^(?:[jt]sx?|mjs|cjs|css|s[ac]ss|less|styl|vue|svelte|astro|mdx?|map|wasm|png|jpe?g|gif|svg|webp|avif|ico|bmp|woff2?|ttf|otf|eot|mp[34]|webm|wav|ogg|m4a)$/i;
// …
server.middlewares.use(function nitroDevMiddlewarePre(req, res, next) {
  const fetchDest = req.headers["sec-fetch-dest"];
  const accept = req.headers["accept"];
  const ext = req.url.match(/\.([a-z0-9]+)(?:[?#]|$)/i)?.[1];
  const isNitroRoute = ext
    ? !!nitro.routing.routes.match(req.method || "", new URL(withBase(req.url, nitro.options.baseURL), "http://localhost").pathname)
    : false;
  const isDocumentLike = fetchDest
    ? /^(document|iframe|frame|empty)$/.test(fetchDest)
    : !(ext && ASSET_EXT_RE.test(ext) && !(typeof accept === "string" && /\btext\/html\b/.test(accept)));
  res.setHeader("vary", "sec-fetch-dest, accept");
  if (isDocumentLike && (!ext || isNitroRoute) && !/^\/(?:__|@)/.test(req.url)) {
    nitroDevMiddleware(req, res, next);
  } else {
    if (!isDocumentLike) req._nitroHandled = true;   // <-- regression
    next();
  }
});
```

Two problems:

1. The condition `if (isDocumentLike && (!ext || isNitroRoute) && …)` already computes `isNitroRoute`, but only consults it under the `isDocumentLike` gate. Asset-extension URLs always fail `isDocumentLike`, so a matching Nitro route can never be reached for them.
2. The `else` branch sets `req._nitroHandled = true` whenever `!isDocumentLike`, regardless of whether a Nitro route exists. The late-stage Nitro fallback registered by the same plugin (`return () => { server.middlewares.use(nitroDevMiddleware); }`) checks this flag and bails out, so even if Vite's static middleware would have fallen through, Nitro never sees the request.

For comparison, in `3.0.1-alpha.2` the same middleware looked like:

```js
server.middlewares.use(function nitroDevMiddlewarePre(req, res, next) {
  const fetchDest = req.headers["sec-fetch-dest"];
  res.setHeader("vary", "sec-fetch-dest");
  if (
    (!fetchDest || /^(document|iframe|frame|empty)$/.test(fetchDest)) &&
    !req.url.match(/\.([a-z0-9]+)(?:[?#]|$)/i)?.[1] &&
    !/^\/(?:__|@)/.test(req.url)
  ) nitroDevMiddleware(req, res, next);
  else next();
});
```

No `_nitroHandled` poisoning, so the late-stage fallback got the request whenever Vite's static middleware fell through.

### Suggested fix

Let a matching Nitro route override the asset-extension shortcut, and don't poison the fallback when one exists:

```js
if ((isDocumentLike || isNitroRoute) && !/^\/(?:__|@)/.test(req.url)) {
  nitroDevMiddleware(req, res, next);
} else {
  if (!isDocumentLike && !isNitroRoute) req._nitroHandled = true;
  next();
}
```

This preserves the optimization (avoid a Nitro round-trip for genuine static-asset URLs) while ensuring user-defined routes always win when they actually match.

### Smoking-gun headers

When the bug fires, the 404 response carries:

```
Content-Security-Policy: default-src 'none'
X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
Content-Type: text/html; charset=utf-8
```

These are the canonical `serve-static@2.x` "not found" headers — handy for confirming whether a 404 came from Vite's static middleware vs Nitro's own routing layer.

